 R←Test_27(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;fns;MyFns;tid;list;fno;crash
⍝ When the error WS cannot be saved, `crash` must survive and say why.
⍝ A thread that is not killed (`killThreads←0`) makes `⎕SAVE` fail.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

⍝ Preconditions...
 #.⎕SHADOW'HandleErrorParms'
 #.HandleErrorParms←##.HandleError.CreateParms
 #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder←GetTempPath⊃⎕SI
 #.HandleErrorParms.killThreads←0
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
 {}'CREATE!'FilesAndDirs.CheckPath #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
 fns←⍎⎕FX'MyFns dummy' '⎕DL 0.1 ⋄ →1'
 tid←fns&1

 ⎕TRAP←(405 'E' '406 ##.HandleError.Process #.HandleErrorParms')(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 :Trap 406
     {⎕SIGNAL ⍵}405
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1
 :EndTrap

 →T.GoToTidyUp 406≠⎕EN
 →T.GoToTidyUp 0≠≢FilesAndDirs.ListFiles #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder,'/*.dws'
 list←FilesAndDirs.ListFiles #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder,'/*.dcf'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 1≠≢list
 fno←(⊃list)⎕FTIE 0
 crash←⎕FREAD fno 1
 ⎕FUNTIE fno
 →T.GoToTidyUp 9≠⎕NC'crash'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 2≠crash.⎕NC'SaveFailed'
 →T.GoToTidyUp 405≢crash.EN                        ⍝ The rest of `crash` is still there

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 ⎕TKILL tid
 {}FilesAndDirs.RmDir #.HandleErrorParms.errorFolder
